      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The effects of the serotonin precursor 5-HTP, were determined in a behavioral DNIC paradigm (increase in vocalization threshold after intraperitoneal injection of the algogenic agent, phenylbenzoquinone). This counter-irritation phenomenon was strongly potentiated by 5-HTP, such potentiation being blocked by the 5-HT receptor blocker, cinanserin. These results are in keeping with those of our recent single unit work in dorsal horn convergent neurons."},
